# 🚀 PART 4 — Install Apache + PHP + MySQL

Now run commands one by one carefully 👇

---

# Step 1: Update Ubuntu

```bash
sudo apt update -y
```

---

# Step 2: Install Apache

```bash
sudo apt install apache2 -y
```

Start Apache:

```bash
sudo systemctl start apache2
```

Restart:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart apache2
```

---

# Step 3: Install PHP

```bash
sudo apt install php libapache2-mod-php php-mysql -y
```

---

# Step 4: Install MySQL Client

```bash
sudo apt install mysql-client -y
```

Check version:

```bash
mysql --version
```

---

# 🚀 PART 5 — Connect EC2 to RDS

Run:

```bash
mysql -h YOUR_RDS_ENDPOINT -u admin -p
```

Example:

```bash
mysql -h mydatabase.abc123.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com -u admin -p
```

Enter password.

If successful:

```text
mysql>
```

🎉 EC2 connected to RDS successfully.

